      "writtenOn": "2019-09-18T08:21:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This comment looks to me like it\u0027s completely out of context. You are referring here to a loop that is in a different function 60 lines above ! And your implementation here has to DEDUCE where it\u0027s called from to behave correctly. I don\u0027t think this is maintainable.\n\nThe fact that you need to do this means the code in this function is dependent on the specific structures of the loops that call it, which is typically a nightmare for maintainability (the code can\u0027t ever be changed, essentially). It\u0027s not really your fault : mostly the problem here is that members are used to pass information between functions called in sequence, which is a well-known anti-pattern, and all you did was to follow the local style.\n\n\nI recommend removing the test here and having prepareDnsTlsMeasurement ALWAYS overwrite whatever happens. Then you move the explanation above where it\u0027s relevant, and if you need any test in the second loop, write the test there.",
