    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3d091937_189a832f",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/connectivity/NetworkDiagnostics.java",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 286,
      "author": {
        "id": 1349423
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-09-19T06:14:54Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "TextUtils.isEmpty(hostname) makes sure we always carry the SNI during SSL handshake if we can, and this function is independent of the loops that call it.\n\nFor example:\nDNS servers: 8.8.8.8\nPrivate DNS servers: 8.8.8.8 (dns.google)\n\nIf we iterate LinkProperties.getDnsServers() and then PrivateDnsCfg.ips:\nprepareIcmpMeasurement(\"8.8.8.8\")\nprepareDnsMeasurement(\"8.8.8.8\")\nprepareDnsTlsMeasurement(null, \"8.8.8.8\")  --- a.1\nprepareDnsTlsMeasurement(\"dns.google\", \"8.8.8.8\")  --- a.2\n\nIf we iterate PrivateDnsCfg.ips and then LinkProperties.getDnsServers():\nprepareDnsTlsMeasurement(\"dns.google\", \"8.8.8.8\")  --- b.1\nprepareIcmpMeasurement(\"8.8.8.8\")\nprepareDnsMeasurement(\"8.8.8.8\")\nprepareDnsTlsMeasurement(null, \"8.8.8.8\")  --- b.2\n\nIf we don\u0027t filter empty hostname, b.1 will be overwritten by b.2, then we are unable to set \"dns.google\" to SNI.",
      "parentUuid": "149b8b71_aea0d70e",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 286,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 286,
        "endChar": 10
      },
      "revId": "5aca484a136f62ef82d4fdfdc1c6e7e2cf0f4d6d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
